  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.328,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "AREAS RELATED TO CIRCLES"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.864,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "155"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.139,
            0.593,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now with this knowledge, let us try to find some relations (or formulae) to calculate their areas.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.183,
            0.593,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let OAPB be a sector of a circle with centre O and radius",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " r "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(see Fig. 11.3). Let the degree measure of",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A O B }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "be",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " q."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.247,
            0.594,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You know that area of a circle (in fact of a circular region or disc) is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "元  r^{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.292,
            0.599,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In a way, we can consider this circular region to be a sector forming an angle of",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i.e., of degree measure 360) at the centre O. Now by applying the Unitary Method, we can arrive at the area of the sector OAPB as follows:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.633,
            0.147,
            0.858,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.633,
                0.147,
                0.858,
                0.319
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.697,
                0.329,
                0.793,
                0.348
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 11.3"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.394,
            0.901,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When degree measure of the angle at the centre is 360, area of the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sector "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\iota = \\pi r ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.432,
            0.901,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, when the degree measure of the angle at the centre is 1, area of the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathtt { s e c t o r } = { \\frac { \\pi r ^ { 2 } } { 3 6 0 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.501,
            0.9,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, when the degree measure of the angle at the centre is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", area of the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{sector} = \\frac{\\pi r^{2}}{360} \\times \\theta = \\frac{\\theta}{360} \\times \\pi r^{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.571,
            0.902,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, we obtain the following relation (or formula) for area of a sector of a circle:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.618,
            0.599,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of the sector of angle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\theta = \\frac{\\theta}{360} \\times \\pi r^{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.667,
            0.807,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "where",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " r "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "is the radius of the circle and",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " q "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the angle of the sector in degrees.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.693,
            0.595,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, a natural question arises : Can we find the length of the arc APB corresponding to this sector? Yes. Again, by applying the Unitary Method and taking the whole length of the circle (of angle 360°) as 2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pr"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", we can obtain the required length of the arc APB as",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\theta } { 3 6 0 } \\times 2 \\pi r"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.837,
            0.682,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, length of an arc of a sector of angle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Theta = \\frac{\\Theta}{360} \\times 2 \\pi r"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.692,
            0.695,
            0.897,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
